🔹 1. What is DAX?
DAX stands for Data Analysis Expressions.

It is a formula language used in Power BI, Power Pivot, and SSAS Tabular models.

Designed to perform data analysis and calculations on data models.

🔹 2. DAX Syntax Basics
DAX formulas always start with an equals sign =.

Use functions, columns, tables, constants, and operators.

dax
Copy
Edit
= SUM(Sales[Total])
🔹 3. Data Types in DAX
Numeric: Integer, Decimal

Boolean: TRUE/FALSE

Text: Strings

Date/Time

Currency

Blank

🔹 4. Calculated Columns vs Measures
Feature	Calculated Column	Measure
Row-by-row context	Yes	No
Stored in model	Yes (consumes memory)	No (calculated on the fly)
Use Case	Used for filtering/sorting	Used for aggregations in visuals

🔹 5. Common DAX Functions
🔸 Aggregation Functions
SUM(), AVERAGE(), MAX(), MIN(), COUNT(), DISTINCTCOUNT()

dax
Copy
Edit
Total Sales = SUM(Sales[Amount])
🔸 Logical Functions
IF(), SWITCH(), AND(), OR(), NOT()

dax
Copy
Edit
Is High Sale = IF(Sales[Amount] > 1000, "Yes", "No")
🔸 Text Functions
CONCATENATE(), LEFT(), RIGHT(), MID(), UPPER(), LOWER(), LEN()

dax
Copy
Edit
Full Name = CONCATENATE(Customer[FirstName], " " & Customer[LastName])
🔸 Date & Time Functions
TODAY(), NOW(), YEAR(), MONTH(), DAY(), DATEDIFF(), DATEADD(), EDATE()

dax
Copy
Edit
Order Age = DATEDIFF(Orders[OrderDate], TODAY(), DAY)
🔸 Filter Functions
FILTER(), ALL(), ALLEXCEPT(), VALUES(), REMOVEFILTERS()

dax
Copy
Edit
Filtered Sales = CALCULATE(SUM(Sales[Amount]), FILTER(Sales, Sales[Region] = "West"))
🔸 Time Intelligence
TOTALYTD(), DATESYTD(), SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR(), PARALLELPERIOD(), DATEADD()

dax
Copy
Edit
YTD Sales = TOTALYTD(SUM(Sales[Amount]), Calendar[Date])
🔹 6. CALCULATE() Function
Most powerful function in DAX

Changes the filter context

dax
Copy
Edit
West Sales = CALCULATE(SUM(Sales[Amount]), Sales[Region] = "West")
🔹 7. Context in DAX
🔸 Row Context
Automatically available in calculated columns

Evaluates expressions row by row

🔸 Filter Context
Comes from reports, slicers, or CALCULATE()

🔹 8. Variables in DAX
Used to simplify complex formulas

